BorrowCapability
├── constructor
│   ├── fixes protocol target, selector, asset and the full health query per implementation
│   ├── receives configuration through ImmutableFactory constructor arguments
│   ├── does not validate or call external targets
│   └── delegated reads obtain dynamic calldata from implementation storage
├── borrow
│   ├── rejects an unset minimum before calling the protocol
│   ├── rejects direct callers and a mismatched selector
│   ├── calls the protocol as the adapter with no intermediate custody
│   ├── callbacks cannot mutate capability configuration or reenter manage
│   └── post-borrow static health query
│       ├── failures, malformed responses, invalid offsets and low health roll back borrowing
│       └── valid health retains funds on the adapter and returns protocol data
├── setMinHealthFactor
│   ├── requires a Merkle-authorized self-call and nonzero minimum
│   ├── sets the initial floor without requiring a separate initializer
│   └── applies updates to subsequent borrowing without enforcing current health
└── replacement and isolation
    ├── removal and replacement preserve the adapter's minimum
    ├── replacement uses the new implementation's protocol configuration and query
    └── adapters sharing an implementation share its fixed query but keep separate minimums
